IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa17-helpers`

-- coa17-part21a-ch2a-notices.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 21A, Chapter 2A -- Duty to notify registrar of
-- persons with significant control (ss 790LA to 790LL; lines 10451-10564 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law,
-- objectively. SOURCE, TARGET and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER are as in coa17-part21-ch1.l4 (JUST TRUE: the text says yes; JUST
-- FALSE: the text says no in its own words; NOTHING: the text does not decide; a caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE).
--
-- THE GATE. Each duty takes `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` (MAYBE BOOLEAN) and a JUST FALSE from it flows
-- through (fork F4). SEAMS: `s 1121 the officer is in default` (the offences); s 12A (the statement of initial significant
-- control, coa1), s 126 (coa3), s 1088 (coa23) and s 1094/s 1096 (coa24) are facts or pointers here. TIME: "within the period
-- of 14 days beginning with the day on which X" has X plus 13 as its last day. Nothing reads today's date.
-- NOT ENCODED HERE (machinery, inert reason 2 in NOTES.md): s 790LI (power to create further duties). Section 790LB(4) is a
-- signpost (inert, reason 1).

-- FORKS in this module (NOTES.md, "Fork register (coa17)", gives each reading and the text that licenses it; the
-- coverage table points each row at its fork): F1 at s 790LA(3), s 790LC(3), s 790LD(3), s 790LE(4), s 790LF(3), s
-- 790LG(2), s 790LH(3), s 790LL(2); F5 at s 790LA(2), s 790LC(2), s 790LD(2), s 790LE(3), s 790LF(2), s 790LG(1A), s
-- 790LH(2); F11 at s 790LJ(1), s 790LL(3); F12 at s 790LE(5) “pre-incorporation change”.

§ `Part 21A Chapter 2A: Duty to notify registrar of persons with significant control`

§§ `Duty to notify registrar of confirmed persons with significant control (s 790LA)`

-- src:10461 | (4) A company is not required to give a notice under this section in relation to a person if—
-- src:10462 | (a) the application for the registration of the company contained a statement of initial significant control naming the person as someone who would, on the company’s incorporation, become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company, and
-- src:10463 | (b) the company has no cause to believe that at any time since its incorporation the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company.
@ref s 790LA(4) A company is not required to give a notice under this section in relation to a person if (src:10461-10463)
GIVEN `the application for registration of the company contained a statement of initial significant control naming the person as someone who would, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has no cause to believe that at any time since its incorporation the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LA(4) the company is not required to give a notice under this section in relation to the person` MEANS
    IF    `the application for registration of the company contained a statement of initial significant control naming the person as someone who would, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity`
       AND `the company has no cause to believe that at any time since its incorporation the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not required to give a notice under this section in relation to a person if" (the if fails)

-- src:10454 | (1) A company must give a notice to the registrar if it has had confirmation of—
-- src:10455 | (a) a person’s status as a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company, and
-- src:10456 | (b) the required particulars of the person (see section 790K).
@ref s 790LA(1) A company must give a notice to the registrar if it has had confirmation (src:10454-10456)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has had confirmation of the person's status as a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has had confirmation of the required particulars of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application for registration of the company contained a statement of initial significant control naming the person as someone who would, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has no cause to believe that at any time since its incorporation the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LA(1) the company must give a notice to the registrar` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF `s 790LA(4) the company is not required to give a notice under this section in relation to the person` `the application for registration of the company contained a statement of initial significant control naming the person as someone who would, on the company's incorporation, become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` `the company has no cause to believe that at any time since its incorporation the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not required to give a notice under this section in relation to a person if" (subsection (4))
         ELSE IF    `the company has had confirmation of the person's status as a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`
                AND `the company has had confirmation of the required particulars of the person`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give a notice to the registrar if it has had confirmation of— (a) ... and (b) ..." (the if fails)

-- src:10457 | (2) A notice under subsection (1) must—
-- src:10458 | (a) contain a statement of the required particulars, and
-- src:10459 | (b) state the date on which the company had confirmation as mentioned in that subsection.
@ref s 790LA(2) A notice under subsection (1) must (src:10457-10459)
GIVEN `the notice contains a statement of the required particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date on which the company had confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LA(2) the notice contains what this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice contains a statement of the required particulars` AND `the notice states the date on which the company had confirmation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (1) must— (a) contain a statement of the required particulars, and (b) state the date on which the company had confirmation" (a bare must not done: fork F5)

-- src:10460 | (3) A notice under subsection (1) must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company had confirmation as mentioned in that subsection.
@ref s 790LA(3) within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company had confirmation (src:10460)
GIVEN `the day on which the company had confirmation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790LA(3) the last day for the company to give the notice to the registrar` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` `the day on which the company had confirmation`

@ref s 790LA(3) the notice was given within the period (src:10460)
GIVEN `the day on which the company had confirmation` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the notice was given to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LA(3) the notice was given to the registrar in time` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` (`s 790LA(3) the last day for the company to give the notice to the registrar` `the day on which the company had confirmation`) `the day on which the notice was given to the registrar` `the day on which the question is asked` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (1) must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company had confirmation"

-- src:10464 | (5) Nothing in section 126 (notice of trusts not receivable by registrar) affects the duty to give a notice under this section (or the receipt of that notice by the registrar).
@ref s 790LA(5) Nothing in section 126 affects the duty to give a notice under this section (src:10464)
GIVEN `the notice is a notice under section 790LA(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LA(5) section 126 affects the duty to give the notice or its receipt by the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the notice is a notice under section 790LA(1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in section 126 (notice of trusts not receivable by registrar) affects the duty to give a notice under this section (or the receipt of that notice by the registrar)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a notice under this section"

§§ `Option to provide ID verification information in notice of change (s 790LB)`

-- src:10466 | (1) A notice under section 790LA(1) that relates to a registrable person may include a statement that the person’s identity is verified (see section 1110A).
@ref s 790LB(1) A notice under section 790LA(1) that relates to a registrable person may include a statement that the person's identity is verified (src:10466)
GIVEN `the notice is a notice under section 790LA(1) that relates to a registrable person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LB(1) the notice may include a statement that the person's identity is verified` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In subsection (1) “registrable person” does not include a person mentioned in section 790C(12)(a) to (d)." (subsection (5))
    ELSE IF `the notice is a notice under section 790LA(1) that relates to a registrable person`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A notice under section 790LA(1) that relates to a registrable person"

-- src:10467 | (2) A notice under section 790LA(1) that relates to a registrable relevant legal entity may include a statement that—
-- src:10468 | (a) specifies the name of one of its relevant officers (within the meaning given by section 790LO(6)) who is an individual and whose identity is verified, and
-- src:10469 | (b) confirms that the individual’s identity is verified.
@ref s 790LB(2) A notice under section 790LA(1) that relates to a registrable relevant legal entity may include a statement that (src:10467-10469)
GIVEN `the notice is a notice under section 790LA(1) that relates to a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LB(2) the notice may include a statement specifying the name of a relevant officer whose identity is verified and confirming that` MEANS
    IF `the notice is a notice under section 790LA(1) that relates to a registrable relevant legal entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A notice under section 790LA(1) that relates to a registrable relevant legal entity"

-- src:10470 | (3) If the notice includes a statement under subsection (2), it must be accompanied by a statement by the individual confirming that the individual is a relevant officer of the registrable relevant legal entity.
@ref s 790LB(3) If the notice includes a statement under subsection (2), it must be accompanied by a statement by the individual (src:10470)
GIVEN `the notice includes a statement under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LB(3) the notice must be accompanied by a statement by the individual confirming that the individual is a relevant officer of the registrable relevant legal entity` MEANS
