         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section requires a company, on its incorporation, to give a notice in relation to a person included in the statement of initial significant control under section 12A." (subsection (4))
         ELSE IF    `the company knows or has cause to believe that a person has become a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`
                AND `the company has not yet had confirmation as mentioned in section 790LA(1)`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give a notice to the registrar if— (a) it knows or has cause to believe ... but (b) it has not yet had confirmation" (the if fails)

