-- src:10499 | (a) the change in the required particulars,
-- src:10500 | (b) the date on which the change occurred, and
-- src:10501 | (c) the date on which the company had confirmation as mentioned in subsection (1).
@ref s 790LE(3) A notice under subsection (1) must state (src:10498-10501)
GIVEN `the notice states the change in the required particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date on which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date on which the company had confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LE(3) the notice states what this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the change in the required particulars` AND `the notice states the date on which the change occurred` AND `the notice states the date on which the company had confirmation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (1) must state— (a) the change in the required particulars, (b) the date on which the change occurred, and (c) the date on which the company had confirmation" (a bare must not done: fork F5)

-- src:10502 | (4) A notice under subsection (1) must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company had confirmation as mentioned in that subsection.
