GIVEN `the day on which the company had confirmation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790LE(4) the last day for the company to give the notice to the registrar` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` `the day on which the company had confirmation`

@ref s 790LE(4) the notice was given within the period (src:10502)
GIVEN `the day on which the company had confirmation` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the notice was given to the registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LE(4) the notice was given to the registrar in time` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` (`s 790LE(4) the last day for the company to give the notice to the registrar` `the day on which the company had confirmation`) `the day on which the notice was given to the registrar` `the day on which the question is asked` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (1) must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company had confirmation"

