§§ `Persons with significant control: offence of failure to notify (s 790LJ)`

-- src:10541 | (1) If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH, or regulations under section 790LI, an offence is committed by—
-- src:10542 | (a) the company, and
-- src:10543 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:10544 | (2) For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 790LJ(1) If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH, or regulations under section 790LI (src:10541-10544)
DECLARE `s 790LJ(1) duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LA`
    `s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LC`
    `s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LD`
    `s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LE`
    `s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LF`
    `s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LG`
    `s 790LJ(1) the duty under section 790LH`
    `s 790LJ(1) the duty under regulations under section 790LI`
    `s 790LJ(1) another duty`

GIVEN `the duty` IS A `s 790LJ(1) duty`
      `the company fails to comply with the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LJ(1)(a) an offence is committed by the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the duty`
    WHEN `s 790LJ(1) another duty` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH, or regulations under section 790LI"
    OTHERWISE
        IF (NOT `the company fails to comply with the duty`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails ... to comply with" (the if fails)
        ELSE IF `the company has a reasonable excuse`
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 790LJ(1)(b) every officer of the company who is in default (src:10543)
GIVEN `the answer under section 790LJ(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LJ(1)(b) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `the answer under section 790LJ(1)(a)` `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:10544 | (2) For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
