§§ `Power of court to order company to remedy defaults or delay (s 790LK)`

-- src:10547 | (1) Where a company makes default in complying with section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH, or regulations under section 790LI, an application may be made to the court for an order requiring the company to deliver to the registrar the information (or statements) necessary to rectify the position.
@ref s 790LK(1) Where a company makes default in complying with section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH (src:10547)
GIVEN `the company makes default in complying with section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH, or regulations under section 790LI` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LK(1) an application may be made to the court for an order requiring the company to deliver the information or statements to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the company makes default in complying with section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH, or regulations under section 790LI`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company makes default in complying with section 790LA, ..." (the where condition fails)

-- src:10548 | (2) The application may be made by—
-- src:10549 | (a) any person aggrieved by the default,
-- src:10550 | (b) any member of the company, or
-- src:10551 | (c) any person who is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company.
@ref s 790LK(2) The application may be made by (src:10548-10551)
GIVEN `the company makes default in complying with section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH, or regulations under section 790LI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a person aggrieved by the default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LK(2) the person may apply to the court` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company makes default in complying with section 790LA, 790LC, 790LD, 790LE, 790LF, 790LG or 790LH, or regulations under section 790LI`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company makes default in complying with section 790LA, ..." (the where condition fails)
    ELSE IF    `the applicant is a person aggrieved by the default`
            OR `the applicant is a member of the company`
            OR `the applicant is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The application may be made by— (a) any person aggrieved by the default, (b) any member of the company, or (c) any person who is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity" does not say "only"

-- src:10552 | (3) On an application under subsection (1) the court may either refuse the application or may make the order and order the company to pay any damages sustained by any party aggrieved.
