    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an application under subsection (1)"

-- src:10556 | (5) Nothing in this section affects a person’s rights under section 1094 or 1096 (rectification of register).
@ref s 790LK(5) Nothing in this section affects a person's rights under section 1094 or 1096 (src:10556)
GIVEN `the right is a right under section 1094 or 1096 (rectification of register)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LK(5) this section affects the person's rights under section 1094 or 1096` MEANS
    IF `the right is a right under section 1094 or 1096 (rectification of register)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects a person’s rights under section 1094 or 1096 (rectification of register)."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person’s rights under section 1094 or 1096"

§§ `Information as to whether information has been delivered (s 790LL)`

-- src:10558 | (1) A person may request a company to tell the person whether all of the information that it is required to deliver to the registrar under this Chapter has been delivered.
@ref s 790LL(1) A person may request a company to tell the person whether all of the information has been delivered (src:10558)
GIVEN `the company is aware that, by virtue of regulations under section 1088, the registrar is required to refrain from making the information available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LL(1) the person may request the company to tell them whether all of the information it is required to deliver under this Chapter has been delivered` MEANS
    IF `the company is aware that, by virtue of regulations under section 1088, the registrar is required to refrain from making the information available for public inspection`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to information if the company is aware that, by virtue of regulations under section 1088, the registrar is required to refrain from making that information available for public inspection" (subsection (5))
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10559 | (2) The company must comply with the request within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the request is made.
@ref s 790LL(2) The company must comply with the request within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the request is made (src:10559)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a request has been made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is aware that, by virtue of regulations under section 1088, the registrar is required to refrain from making the information available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LL(2) the company must comply with the request` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF (NOT `a request has been made under subsection (1)`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must comply with the request" (no request has been made)
         ELSE IF `the company is aware that, by virtue of regulations under section 1088, the registrar is required to refrain from making the information available for public inspection`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to information if the company is aware that" (subsection (5))
              ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 790LL(2) within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the request is made (src:10559)
GIVEN `the day on which the request is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790LL(2) the last day for the company to comply with the request` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` `the day on which the request is made`

@ref s 790LL(2) the company complied within the period (src:10559)
GIVEN `the day on which the request is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company complied with the request` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LL(2) the company complied with the request in time` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` (`s 790LL(2) the last day for the company to comply with the request` `the day on which the request is made`) `the day on which the company complied with the request` `the day on which the question is asked` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must comply with the request within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the request is made"

-- src:10560 | (3) If the company fails, without reasonable excuse, to do so, an offence is committed by—
-- src:10561 | (a) the company, and
-- src:10562 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 790LL(3) If the company fails, without reasonable excuse, to do so, an offence is committed (src:10560-10562)
GIVEN `the answer under section 790LL(2) that the company complied in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LL(3)(a) an offence is committed by the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 790LL(2) that the company complied in time`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company fails, without reasonable excuse, to do so" (it did not fail)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        IF `the company has a reasonable excuse`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the company has not yet failed

@ref s 790LL(3)(b) every officer of the company who is in default (src:10560-10562)
GIVEN `the answer under section 790LL(3)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LL(3)(b) an offence is committed by the officer of the company who is in default` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold` `the answer under section 790LL(3)(a)` `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:10563 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 790LL(4) liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale (src:10563)
`s 790LL(4) the penalty` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS 3, `fraction of the level` IS 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- src:10564 | (5) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to information if the company is aware that, by virtue of regulations under section 1088, the registrar is required to refrain from making that information available for public inspection.
@ref s 790LL(5) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to information if the company is aware that the registrar is required to refrain (src:10564)
GIVEN `the company is aware that, by virtue of regulations under section 1088, the registrar is required to refrain from making the information available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790LL(5) subsection (1) does not apply to the information` MEANS
    IF `the company is aware that, by virtue of regulations under section 1088, the registrar is required to refrain from making the information available for public inspection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to information if the company is aware that, by virtue of regulations under section 1088, the registrar is required to refrain from making that information available for public inspection"
